<Layout title="Public life — Andreas Andreou" description="Public service, local government and European policy through the experience of Galatsi.">
  <section class="story-hero wrap"><img src="/assets/galatsi-civic-collage.png" alt="Civic life in Galatsi" /><div class="story-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Public contribution</span><h1>Policy becomes real when someone is waiting for an answer.</h1><p class="lede">Local government is where good intentions meet procedures, budgets, suppliers and the everyday expectations of citizens.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Galatsi · Athens</span></div><div><h2>Close to the consequences.</h2><p>As a Municipal Councillor and former Deputy Mayor responsible for the Press Office, I learned that communication is inseparable from the institution behind it. A request that looks simple from the outside may cross departments, systems and constraints before it reaches a citizen.</p><p>That experience sharpened my interest in procurement, digital government and the practical design of public institutions — not as abstract policy, but as systems people encounter. During this period, I helped oversee the transfer of the Galatsi Olympic Hall, securing €1.2m in annual municipal income through commercial leases and enabling savings and land acquisitions for future green urban space.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap"><span class="eyebrow">What public service taught me</span><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Implementation is policy.</h3><p>The quality of a decision is tested by whether an institution can deliver it.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Trust is operational.</h3><p>Clear communication and visible accountability are part of how institutions work.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Local insight scales.</h3><p>What happens in a municipality can reveal lessons for wider public systems.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="section band"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">From local experience to better systems</span><h2>Public value is built one practical decision at a time.</h2><a class="button" href="/#contact">Start a conversation ↗</a></div></section>
</Layout>
